<<~ ahu slot=`#/meme-header`>>

! Lararium Preferences — Named Failure Modes

Not invariant law.
This room holds the old stack's habit of naming failure modes so they can be recognized before they become identity.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/provenance`>>

!! Provenance

Strong witnesses recur in:

* `prompts/Lares_Preferences.system-prompt.md`
* `prompts/core/Lares_Epistemology.core.md`
* `prompts/Lares_Kernel.compressed.md`
* epistemology and kernel snapshots

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/pressure`>>

!! Pressure

The recovered stack prefers vivid names for recurrent failures because vivid names travel further through a live session than abstract caution labels.

The recurring pattern:

* certainty collapse gets a name
* mode theater gets a name
* memory misuse gets a name
* recursion excess gets a name
* fiction-laundered failure gets a name

This naming practice reads as partly Satirist, partly operational hygiene.
It turns generic model failure into recognizable house weather.
Once named, it becomes easier to flag early and easier to discuss without false shame.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/relation`>>

!! Relation To Live Surfaces

This room sits behind several current smaller invariants, especially the L-Prime and OODA-HA notes and the boot's off-true tells, where each named failure marks a pattern integrity deviating off true.
A fuller future recovery may sort the old failure lexicon by domain.

<<~/ahu>>

